1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:03,999
The brush clears a stone boat, with a tall mast.

2
00:00:03,999 --> 00:00:10,774
It stands for the port of Mamallapuram, where Pallava kings carved temples out of single rocks, beside the sea.

3
00:00:10,774 --> 00:00:13,508
Why carve a temple out of one rock?

4
00:00:32,317 --> 00:00:41,527
How do we know? Pallava copper plates and stone inscriptions give lists of kings. Archaeologists dug up the port at Mamallapuram.

5
00:00:41,527 --> 00:00:46,081
The Tamil hymns of the Nayanars and Alvars describe the age.

6
00:01:03,383 --> 00:01:08,673
The Pallavas ruled from Kanchipuram, about the sixth to the ninth century CE.

7
00:01:08,673 --> 00:01:15,242
Simhavishnu, about 575 CE, defeated the Kalabhras and began the great age.

8
00:01:15,242 --> 00:01:22,626
His son Mahendravarman the First was a patron of rock-cut temples, and wrote a comic play, the Mattavilasa Prahasana.

9
00:01:22,626 --> 00:01:32,465
Narasimhavarman the First, called Mamalla, defeated the Chalukya king Pulakeshin the Second, and took his capital, Vatapi, in 642 CE.

10
00:01:32,465 --> 00:01:40,651
He founded Mamallapuram. There, the Pancha Rathas are five temples carved from single rocks, with chariot-like shapes.

11
00:01:40,651 --> 00:01:46,996
The Shore Temple, built by Rajasimha, is a structural temple of stone blocks, beside the sea.

12
00:01:46,996 --> 00:01:51,175
At Kanchipuram, Rajasimha built the Kailasanatha temple.

13
00:01:51,175 --> 00:02:00,022
In these centuries, the bhakti poets, the Nayanars and Alvars, sang in Tamil. Their songs carried devotion to the people.

14
00:02:17,317 --> 00:02:25,018
Old name, new name. The Pallava port is called Mamallapuram, after Mamalla, the title of Narasimhavarman.

15
00:02:25,018 --> 00:02:29,860
The modern name of the town is Mahabalipuram, and both names are in use.

16
00:02:47,150 --> 00:02:54,632
Carve this tip into memory. Pallava: rathas, Shore Temple. Kanchi, Mamalla.

17
00:02:54,632 --> 00:02:59,608
Remember the rock-cut chariots and the Shore Temple, and name Mamalla as the founder.

18
00:03:16,917 --> 00:03:33,832
Dig Quiz. Pause and name it. Number one. Which seaside temple was built by Rajasimha? The answer: the Shore Temple. Number two.

19
00:03:33,832 --> 00:03:53,432
How many rathas stand at Mamallapuram? The answer: five. Number three. Name the Pallava capital. The answer: Kanchipuram.

20
00:03:53,432 --> 00:04:00,192
Now one line for Mains. Discuss the contribution of the Pallavas to art and architecture.

21
00:04:21,483 --> 00:04:30,600
The boat goes into its case. It recalls the port beside the Shore Temple. Three facts to take away. A boat of the Pallava port.

22
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:40,548
Mamallapuram, 7th century CE. Rock-cut rathas and a Shore Temple. Next gallery: The Chalukyas of Badami.

